# Build-context exclusions for both Dockerfile.api and Dockerfile.dashboard.
#
# The local MLflow registry (mlruns.db, mlartifacts/) and local datasets
# (data/*) are never copied into either image. Phase 15: the images instead
# get the committed packaged registered model (models/registered/, allowed
# below) and regenerate data/processed/customer_features.parquet at build
# time from the committed, seeded pipeline -- so the build is identical on
# any machine and never picks up stale or machine-specific local state.

.git/
.github/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
mlruns/
mlartifacts/
*.db
*.pkl
*.joblib
# .dockerignore globs match from the context root only (unlike .gitignore),
# so the patterns above miss nested files such as models/*.joblib -- these
# recursive forms exclude them everywhere.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
**/*.db
**/*.pkl
**/*.joblib
# Phase 15: the packaged registered model the API loads (see .gitignore).
!models/registered/*/*/model.pkl
catboost_info/

# Regenerated inside the image at build time -- see note above.
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/external/

# Large generated inference output (~50MB+), never needed by the API or
# dashboard containers (matches .gitignore).
reports/customer_recommendations.csv

# Not needed inside either running container.
notebooks/
tests/
